## Five tiers of slot vocabulary

Per the tag-modeling-first-class ADR, the slot vocabulary forms five tiers:

- **Tier A — Identity**: value (canonical form), alt-labels (synonyms), hidden-labels (search-only)
- **Tier B — Documentation**: definition, scope-note, example, editorial-note, change-note, history-note
- **Tier C — Concept relations**: broader-generic, broader-instantial, broader-partitive, related, in-scheme
- **Tier D — Lifecycle**: vocabulary-level (free / canonical), lifecycle-status, superseded-by, category-type, canonical?
- **Tier E — Federation + provenance + validation**: introduced-in, constraints, sort-key, exact-match, close-match, broader-match, narrower-match, related-match

